Chapter: Utf8CceTest
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 The UTF-8 boundary in Foreword chapter CCE. tools/cdx-store
 converted a wire byte at a time through from-unicode, which is correct only
 over the single-byte range and wrong without saying so above it.

   three-byte CJK  old: 3 characters   new: 1 character
   two-byte e-acute old: 1 character   new: 1 character
                    old: code point 361  new: code point 233

 So the character count catches the three- and four-byte cases and CANNOT catch
 the two-byte one -- the old path drops one byte, maps the other, and lands on a
 single character that is simply the wrong one. U+00E9 came out as U+0169: an
 e-acute silently became a u-double-acute. That is why every case here asserts
 the code point as well as the count. An assertion that cannot fail on the code
 it replaces is not evidence, and the count alone was exactly that.

Section: Helpers

  u8-bytes-equal : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  u8-bytes-equal (a) (b) (i) =
    if list-length a == list-length b then
      if i >= list-length a then True
      else if list-at a i == list-at b i then u8-bytes-equal a b (i + 1)
      else False
    else False

  u8-check : Boolean, Text -> Text
  u8-check (ok) (label) = label & "=" & if ok then "pass" else "fail"

 A decoded character is read back out through to-unicode, so the test never
 hardcodes a CCE code -- it asserts the Unicode code point that went in is the
 one that comes out. It is read with cce-decode-at and not char-code, because
 Text is a byte sequence: char-code would hand back the lead byte of a
 multi-byte CCE character rather than the character.

  u8-cp-of : List Integer -> Integer
  u8-cp-of (bytes) =
    let t = utf8-bytes-to-text bytes
    in if text-length t == 0 then -1 else to-unicode (cce-decode-at t 0)

  u8-char-count : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  u8-char-count (t) (i) (len) (n) =
    if i >= len then n
    else u8-char-count t (i + cce-decode-length (char-code (char-at t i))) len (n + 1)

  u8-chars-of : List Integer -> Integer
  u8-chars-of (bytes) =
    let t = utf8-bytes-to-text bytes
    in u8-char-count t 0 (text-length t) 0

  u8-len-of : List Integer -> Integer
  u8-len-of (bytes) = text-length (utf8-bytes-to-text bytes)

Section: Body

  u8-ascii : List Integer = [72, 101, 108, 108, 111]
  u8-e-acute : List Integer = [195, 169]
  u8-cjk : List Integer = [228, 184, 173]
  u8-emoji : List Integer = [240, 159, 152, 128]

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-chars-of u8-ascii == 5) "utf8-ascii-len")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-cp-of u8-ascii == 72) "utf8-ascii-cp")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-chars-of u8-e-acute == 1) "utf8-2byte-one-char")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-cp-of u8-e-acute == 233) "utf8-2byte-cp")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-chars-of u8-cjk == 1) "utf8-3byte-one-char")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-cp-of u8-cjk == 20013) "utf8-3byte-cp")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-chars-of u8-emoji == 1) "utf8-4byte-one-char")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-cp-of u8-emoji == 128512) "utf8-4byte-cp")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (utf8-decode-length 65 == 1) "utf8-lead-ascii")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (utf8-decode-length 169 == 0) "utf8-lead-continuation")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-len-of [195] == 0) "utf8-truncated-dropped")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-len-of [169] == 0) "utf8-stray-cont-dropped")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-len-of u8-cjk == 2) "utf8-3byte-cce-bytes")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-bytes-equal (text-to-utf8-bytes (utf8-bytes-to-text u8-cjk)) u8-cjk 0) "utf8-roundtrip-3byte")
    print-line-uni (u8-check (u8-bytes-equal (text-to-utf8-bytes (utf8-bytes-to-text u8-emoji)) u8-emoji 0) "utf8-roundtrip-4byte")
  end
